  ⚠ scriptc(promise-all-inline-tuple): inline `Promise.all([...])` infers a tuple type; tuple edges are fenced
   ╭─[promise_all_inline_tuple.tsx:1:17]
 1 │ const r = await Promise.all([work(1), work(2)]);
   ·                 ───────────────────────────────
   ╰────
  help: Type the array first: `const jobs: Promise<number>[] = [...]; await Promise.all(jobs);` — see the scriptc limitations page on tuple inference.

